  "2026-10-23T20:00:10.085Z",codex-agent,"Complete release verification at 6fba6b0 in CI run 40012369395: npm run release:check on Node 22 passed 760/760; npm run release:check on Node 26 passed 760/760; bun run release:check on Node 26 passed 760/760. Each measured all 51 source files at 100% statements/lines/branches/functions, zero test failures/skips. Strict tracker health, identity/privacy, production audit, package dry run and changelog checks passed; CodeQL passed. Earlier local subprocess timing failures passed unchanged on focused retry (2/2) and all full CI gates. Broad linked runner timeout was replaced by focused 5/5 passes; both complete files pass in full CI. Stopped remaining duplicate local gate after complete CI acceptance; no local full-gate pass is claimed. Six independent assertion-failing behavioural reverts are recorded above. No review threads were replied to or resolved; CodeRabbit skipped review and Greptile reported an expired trial. The item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-23T20:00:12.513Z",codex-agent,"Bookkeeping: one file-link event used the detected harness:codex identity before the explicit author export; later writes explicitly use codex-agent. Existing history was preserved append-only. No history repair or re-anchoring was performed."
  "2026-10-23T20:21:38.649Z",codex-agent,"Final-head CI exposed a separate staging TOCTOU race: Node 22 passed 759/760 but the checkpoint-only Compose case failed when completion.json disappeared between readdir and lstat in stagingBytes. This is an actual filesystem race, not a timeout; fixing it within release-gate recovery. Missing listed entries now contribute zero current retained bytes, while missing staging directories, links/directories and missing completion receipts still refuse. Added a real-filesystem deletion at the enumeration boundary with no SDK mock."
  "2026-10-23T20:23:12.584Z",codex-agent,"Staging race regression passes 2/2 with existing completion-integrity coverage on both Node 22 and Node 26: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"staging measurement|completion validation refuses\" test/process.test.ts. Reverting only stagingBytes to its previous lstat behavior makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"staging measurement\" test/process.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1, with ERR_ASSERTION from the real ENOENT. Restored the exact source immediately. The test removes an actual completion file after native directory enumeration, checks retained-byte accounting, and still requires the typed missing-receipt refusal. No SDK mock or timing-based race is used. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass."
  "2026-10-23T20:25:11.185Z",codex-agent,"Read every failed check in CI run 40015852948 with gh run view --log-failed: one Node 22 staging-entry deletion race (759/760) was the sole failure; npm Node 26 and Bun passed 760/760 with full 100% coverage. The race is now fixed in stagingBytes with a native nonthrowing missing-entry stat; other filesystem errors and unsafe entries still fail. Linked staging tests pass 2/2, as do direct Node 22/26 runs, and the seventh independent behavioural revert fails deterministically. Build, typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring checks pass. Seven revert proofs and 5/5 policy/history plus 2/2 staging linked results are retained. Final release CI will validate the next pushed head at unchanged thresholds; no new permission or review authority is implied."
  "2026-10-23T21:00:46.657Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched remote head 0a46d8e; main is fully included. Complete GraphQL reviewThreads read returned zero threads; no CodeRabbit review body or outside-diff findings exists (automatic review skipped). Verified both supplied blockers: minimizing scores are treated as regressions, and prospective approval citations can overflow a card after promotion commits. Plan: direction-aware regression classification and in-lock prospective-card validation before promotion writes; regressions and independent behavioural revert proofs, full unchanged npm/Bun release gates. SDK pin remains unchanged; current registry CLI is 2026.10.23."
  "2026-10-23T21:04:12.509Z",codex-agent,"Implemented shared prospective export validation inside the promotion writer lock, before update/close; the promoted body contributes approval citations, numeric limits, direction-aware regressions and outcome bytes. Both manual and recursive promotion callers use this core. Self-review found one generation regression comparison and no second irreversible promotion writer. Direction regression passes for minimizing/maximizing improvements, ties and regressions. A separate long-identifier SDK lock refusal discovered during fixture construction is tracked by pm-rl-longidlock; no upstream report filed."
  "2026-10-23T21:05:16.441Z",codex-agent,"Two independent behavioural reverts proved the fixes: (1) restoring only the maximization comparison in source makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"policy regressions respect\" test/policy-card.test.ts fail 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION (reward_regression incorrectly emitted for minimizing improvement); (2) removing only the in-lock validatePromotedPolicyCard call makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"prospective promoted card overflow\" test/policy-card.test.ts fail 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION because candidate body changed to promoted despite card_limit. Each exited 1; production source restored in finally; test SHA-256 unchanged. Restored direction scenarios passed 1/1 and overflow passed 1/1: two failed attempts preserve body/status/updated_at/card digest, then a smaller candidate consumes the same one-unit approval and retains a replayable promoted card. Tests import source; dist is untracked."
  "2026-10-23T21:05:33.229Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test pm-rl-policycards --run --only-last --progress passed both new regressions, 2/2, zero failures/skips/cancellations, in its snapshot workspace with PM context none. Full release gate is running with isolated HOME and global/system Git configuration disabled, Node 26, at the unchanged four 100-percent thresholds. npm ci completed with zero audit vulnerabilities. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplication (zero clones across 51 files), docstrings (378 declarations), and changelog generation/check passed. No CodeRabbit finding was available to reject; no GitHub review thread exists to reply to or resolve."
  "2026-10-23T21:26:57.545Z",codex-agent,"Bun release gate passed in CI run 40024257594 at code head 28ca37cd221267a9ee5d62cb574e57f743f971a4: bun run release:check, Node 26, 763/763 tests, zero failures/skips, all 51 source files at 100 percent statements/lines/branches/functions. Strict tracker health, typecheck/build, lint, zero duplication, 378 documented declarations, publish attestation, identity audit, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog check passed. CodeQL passed in run 40024257587. npm Node 22/26 jobs remain running. Stopped the duplicate local npm gate intentionally after 127 reported passing cases and no reported failure to reduce shared host load; no local full-gate pass is claimed."
  "2026-10-23T21:34:58.134Z",codex-agent,"Complete unchanged release gates passed at code head 28ca37cd221267a9ee5d62cb574e57f743f971a4 in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/40024257594 : npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26 and bun run release:check on Node 26 each passed 763/763 tests, zero failures/skips. All 51 source files measured 100 percent statements/lines/branches/functions in each job. Strict tracker health, identity and production audits, lint/duplication/docstrings, build, publish attestation, package dry run and changelog checks passed. CodeQL passed. Both new regressions passed 2/2 through pinned pm test, and both independent behavioural reverts failed 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION as recorded above. No timeout or failure occurred in these full CI runs; the duplicate local gate was intentionally stopped and is not a full pass. No new review threads appeared. Final follow-up commit contains tracker receipts only; no code change after full CI acceptance. The item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; no merge, release, review reply or thread resolution."
  "2026-10-23T21:50:37.110Z",codex-agent,"Third independent review confirmed both blockers: replay accepts unrelated certified citations and registration validates limits after generation/history creation. GraphQL returned zero review threads (no pagination); no CodeRabbit review body exists, and its issue comment records automatic review skipped. Plan: bind historical citations to the certified subject dependency graph, preflight complete cards before durable writes, audit every added write including receipts and budgets, and prove refusal atomicity with complete tracker byte snapshots plus independent behavioural reverts. Earlier fixes remain required. Remote branch is current and contains main; no merge needed."
  "2026-10-23T21:58:27.907Z",codex-agent,"Write-boundary audit found additional instances: batch card publication could write a shared card before a selected-card collision; outer recursive phase receipts and checkpoint artifacts were persisted before card-limit checks; rejection notes/comments and recovery closes also needed preflight. These now validate before the associated durable write. Promotion retains its authoritative in-lock validation and gains a pre-journal check. Registration defers schema initialization too. Snapshot tests include all durable domain/history/budget/artifact/journal files; the pinned SDK unconditionally appends derived runtime/context-usage.jsonl on ordinary get calls, and active controller locks renew, so only that derived ledger and ephemeral locks are explicitly excluded. This SDK read-side effect is a concrete UX gap; no telemetry setting or SDK dependency changed."
  "2026-10-23T22:00:09.924Z",codex-agent,"Focused regression run passed 6/6 with zero failures, cancellations or skips: unrelated certified citation forgery, both registration bounds, pre-journal promotion overflow and unchanged approval capacity, batch collision before partial publication, recursive receipt plus checkpoint publication preflight, and rejection-note preflight. Both count and byte-limit registration refusals were retried twice. Every refusal comparison enumerates and compares all durable files, including histories and transaction/artifact receipts, with the two explicitly documented SDK-derived exclusions. The write inventory is docs/policy-card-write-audit.md. Behavioural reverts and full unchanged npm/Bun release gates are next."
  "2026-10-23T22:03:39.871Z",codex-agent,"Seven isolated function-only revert cases are being exercised on text-only source copies with the same pinned SDK and unchanged regression file: foreign citation validation, registration preflight, pre-journal promotion check, batch collision preflight, receipt intent deferral, artifact pre-publication validation, and rejection-note validation. The first five already fail with ERR_ASSERTION as required. Final self-review also excludes allowances from plans and comparison receipts (they do not declare resource budgets), and rejects extra wrapper fields on the pinned Plan. The initial local npm gate was stopped before its test run to include this final hardening; no full pass is claimed for that superseded run. New baseline gates will run on frozen source."
  "2026-10-23T22:04:29.499Z",codex-agent,"All seven behavioural reverts failed 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1, while the regression file hash stayed unchanged within each source-only reversion. Cases: foreign-citation allowlist, registration preflight, pre-journal promotion preflight, batch collision preflight, receipt intent deferral, artifact pre-publication callback, rejection-note preflight. Each modified production file was restored in finally. Source-based tests need no dist rebuild; dist is untracked and rebuilt by release gates. Literal full-file equality is separately tracked by pm-rl-readusage because current SDK reads append a derived usage ledger. Full isolated-identity tracker health passed; default HOME health reports a local pm-github host-version skew, without history drift. The pinned pm test metadata update also refuses guarded item-format 2 because the existing peer floor includes older hosts; no pin or history was changed. Runtime context and timeout overrides are being used for the required pm test runner."
  "2026-10-23T22:07:47.684Z",codex-agent,"Required pinned PM execution passed: pm test pm-rl-policycards --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 --pm-context none --override-linked-pm-context --workspace-context snapshot --override-linked-workspace-context ran the six-boundary regression command successfully, 6/6 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations, exit 0, 214.256 seconds. This follows an unrelated default-schema initialization refusal; the explicit supported runtime context override is the successful evidence. TypeScript source and test typechecks passed. The full npm release gate is measuring the frozen source; Bun and Node floor acceptance will also run through the existing CI matrix."
